{"url": "https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/education/graduate/phd/financial-aid", "final_url": "https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/education/graduate/phd/financial-aid", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-24", "text": "Financial Aid - PhD Programs - Graduate Education - Education - URochester Medicine\nSkip to main content\nSchool of Medicine & Dentistry\nmenu\nMedical Education\nAdmissions\nNewsletter\nIncoming Students\nCurrent Students\nMD/PhD Program\nPolicies\nVisiting Students\nAlumni\nHigh School and Undergraduate Programs\nLearn More About Medical Education\nGraduate Education\nProspective Students\nCurrent Students\nNon-Matriculated Students\nmyHub\nResearch Ethics\nSummer Scholars Program\nTrainee Handbook\nForms\nRegistrar\nAlumni\nContact Us\nLearn More About Graduate Education\nResidency & Fellowship\nLiving in Rochester\nProspective Residents\nProspective Fellows\nOrientation\nEligibility Requirements\nBenefits\nContact Us\nLearn More about Residency & Fellowship\nPostdoctoral Affairs\nmyHub\nNational Postdoc Appreciation Week\nPostdoctoral Association\nPostdoctoral Jobs\nTrainee Handbook\nForms\nResearch Ethics\nLearn More about Postdoctoral Affairs\nOther Programs\nNursing\nDental\nContinuing Medical Education\nLearn More about Other Programs\nOffices\nRegistrar\nBursar's Office\nFinancial Aid Office\nDean's Office\nCurriculum Assessment\nLearn More About Administrative Offices\nPhD Programs\nHome\n2027 Discover URSMD Weekend\nApplication Deadlines\nContacts\nEducational Opportunities\nFinancial Aid\nFrequently Asked Questions\nHow To Apply\nInquiry Form\nLiving in Rochester\nEducation /\nGraduate Education /\nPhD Programs /\nFinancial Aid\nFinancial Aid\nPhD Applicants\nFellowship Package for Full-time Students\nFull tuition scholarship, including all academic fees. Tuition and Fee Schedule\nA competitive stipend for 2027-2028 of $35,800 per year for 12-month programs or $29,833 per year for 10-month programs.\nSingle coverage AETNA student health insurance policy.\nRefund Schedule\nHealth Insurance\nThe University Health Service(UHS) provides a full range of confidential, high-quality primary health care services for full-time students and other members of the University community.\nFull-time students participate in the Student Health Program, which covers primary care visits to UHS, time-limited therapy at the University Counseling Center (UCC), and health promotion services.\nUHS offers health insurance for individual full-time University of Rochester students and their spouses/domestic partners through AETNA. Full-time students are required to participate in this plan unless they complete the Health Insurance Selection Process indicating they are waiving the insurance plan because they have other insurance. Insurance for spouses/partners and families is available for a fee payable by the student.\nChildcare Program\nThe University of Rochester is implementing a pilot childcare grant program for full-time PhD students on university appointments who are parents of children newborn through age 6 (\u201cstudent-parents\u201d). The objective of this program is to provide some financial assistance to Rochester PhD students with childcare expenses. Additional details can be found at https://www.rochester.edu/graduate-education/phd-students/childcare-grant/.\nRelated Departments\nThe Bursar\u2019s Office\nFinancial Aid Office\nFind Us on Social\nInformation\nAbout Us\nOur Hospitals\nDepartments and Centers\nNewsroom\nJob Opportunities\nContact Information\nTools\nEvent Calendar\nFind a Physician\nHealth Encyclopedia\nFaculty Lists\nMyChart Patient Portal\nOnline Bill Pay\nGeneral Information\nUniversity of Rochester\nWeb Accessibility\nFaculty & Staff Directory\nEmergency Information\n\u00a92026 University of Rochester Medical Center Rochester, NY\nIntranet\nEmail\nmyURHR\nRemote Access (VPN)\nPrivacy Topics\nViewing: UrmcWebTest", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/educa